@baseUrl = http://localhost:5206

### All screenings
GET {{baseUrl}}/screenings

### One screening
GET {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1

### Screening that does not exist -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/screenings/999

### Valid reservation -> 200 and a receipt
POST {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada",
  "seatNumber": 6
}

### Same seat again -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Grace",
  "seatNumber": 6
}

### Seat number out of range -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada",
  "seatNumber": 99
}

### Missing name -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "",
  "seatNumber": 7
}

### Screening that does not exist -> 404 (was 400 before challenge 1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/screenings/999/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada",
  "seatNumber": 1
}

### Fifth seat for the same customer -> 409 (run the four below first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Ada",
  "seatNumber": 7
}

### Cancel your own reservation -> 200 and the released seat
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations/6?customerName=Ada

### Cancel a seat somebody else holds -> 409
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations/2?customerName=Ada

### Cancel a seat that is not reserved -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations/7?customerName=Ada

### Cancel a seat number that does not exist -> 400
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/screenings/1/reservations/99?customerName=Ada
